       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's double the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release tablets in adults. The limit is 2,000 mg/day for most extended-release products. A dose that high raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nThe 1700 mg may be a typo. Here are some standard options:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg or 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is a lower starting or titration dose.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or give me a different intended dose, and I'll enter it right away. If the patient is already on a regimen you're trying to match, tell me that too, and we can sort out the right dose."
