       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the labeled maximum, and I can't verify the label claim from here. The FDA-approved maximum for adults is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Some extended-release products have a lower limit of 2,000 to 2,500 mg/day. An order of 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is above all of those limits.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum)\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **Another dose at or below the labeled maximum**\n\nIf you think the label allows a higher dose, check the current prescribing information or ask pharmacy to review it. If there's a clinical reason to go above the label, that has to go through pharmacy or the prescriber of record. I can't enter it myself. Which of these do you want?"
